    Call 1: ('In open62541/src/server/ua_services_session.c Service_ActivateSession and open62541/src/server/ua_session.c UA_Session_attachToSecureChannel, what is the safest minimal root-cause fix for repeated activation on the same channel? Should Service_ActivateSession skip attach when session->header.channel == channel, or should UA_Session_attachToSecureChannel itself be made idempotent (and perhaps handle migration)? Identify expected invariants and all callers.', 'The supplied ASan report demonstrates that a second successful ActivateSession for the same UA_Session on the same UA_SecureChannel calls UA_Session_attachToSecureChannel twice. The intrusive UA_SessionHeader list entry is inserted twice, corrupting the channel sessions list. Session removal detaches once, delayed destruction frees the session, and later UA_SecureChannel_deleteMembersCleanup traverses the stale list entry and causes a heap-use-after-free. I have observed Service_ActivateSession lines 267-275 only detach when the existing channel differs and then unconditionally attach. A reference search found the attach function is only called from Service_ActivateSession, but I want to preserve valid reactivation and channel transfer semantics and choose the strongest invariant-enforcing location.')...
