    Call 3: ('Trace every way in this exact open62541 tree that UA_SessionManager_removeSession/removeSession can be invoked for an attached session, and every delayed callback/channel-close ordering that could cause the same session to be freed before UA_SecureChannel_deleteMembersCleanup. Look especially for duplicate removeSession scheduling, malformed list behavior, CloseSession handling, SecureChannel close, and shutdown ordering. Identify another root cause compatible with a UAF remaining even after both Service_ActivateSession skips attach when `session->header.channel == channel` and UA_Session_attachToSecureChannel itself has the same idempotence guard.', "I implemented two prevention layers in open62541: ua_session.c's attach helper returns immediately if already attached to the passed channel, and ua_services_session.c now calls attach only in a `session->header.channel != channel` branch while preserving activation and lifetime refresh. Yet test_patch twice reports the supplied PoV still crashes with the exact dedup UA_SecureChannel_deleteMembersCleanup -> manager cleanup -> server delete, with the session freed by removeSessionCallback during shutdown. The PoV includes HEL/OPN, Create/Activate, then additional Create/Activate-looking traffic and CLO. We need identify why a stale channel list pointer survives one detach despite duplicate insertion now prevented, or whether another insertion/build source exists.")...
